// @test: differential
// @tier: 0,1
// @level: L0
// @tags: aot, codegen, context, text, tier-parity, regression
// @timeout: 60000
// @expected-exit: 0
// @expected-stdout-begin
// via-context: row-42
// returned: row-42
// count: 7
// @expected-stdout-end
//
// Regression guard for T1210: a `Text` returned by a CONTEXT method must
// keep its type, so an f-string prints the TEXT and not its pointer.
//
// THE SHAPE, and the second line is what makes the site identifiable.
// The SAME value is printed twice — once inside the function that got it
// from the context, once after it is returned to `main`:
//
//     tier 0   via-context: row-42        returned: row-42
//     tier 1   via-context: 4381999968    returned: row-42
//
// The value is intact. What differs is the PATH TO THE FORMAT. `main`'s
// print works because `use_db`'s own declared return type is `Text` and
// the `Call` arm stamps that; the first print fails because the value
// came from a `CallM` on a `CtxGet` receiver, and `lower_ctx_get`
// (`instruction.rs`) stores its result with `set_register` and stamps NO
// type at all. An untyped receiver cannot resolve a method, an
// unresolved method has no return type, and the `CallM` arm applies a
// mark only when it has one — so the `Text` reaches `ToString` as a bare
// i64 and prints as its address.
//
// `count: 7` IS THE CONTROL AND IT MUST NOT MOVE. An `Int` returned by a
// context method prints correctly WITHOUT any mark, so it cannot show
// this defect — which is exactly why it belongs here: a fix that stamps
// the wrong type would read a scalar as a heap pointer and crash, and
// this line is what says it did not. Its passing is not evidence that
// the path is healthy; only the `Text` line can be.
//
// DIFFERENTIAL, because the interpreter is right here and always has
// been (Tier 0 values self-describe through NaN-boxing, so no codegen
// mark is involved). A tier-1-only assertion would pass the day someone
// broke Tier 0 instead, and the two tiers AGREEING is the property.
//
// NOT T1206, measured rather than assumed: on the binary that fixed
// T1206 and made `docs/by-example/04-result-error` agree between tiers,
// this shape was unchanged. Same symptom — an address where text
// belongs — three different causes. They converge at `ToString` by
// construction, since an unmarked `Text` and an `Int` are the same i64
// there.

mount core.prelude.*;

context Db {
    fn fetch(id: Int) -> Text;
    fn tally() -> Int;
}

type FakeDb is { prefix: Text };

implement FakeDb {
    public fn fetch(&self, id: Int) -> Text { f"{self.prefix}-{id}" }
    public fn tally(&self) -> Int { 7 }
}

fn use_db() -> Text using [Db] {
    let row = Db.fetch(42);
    print(f"via-context: {row}");
    row
}

fn main() {
    let db = FakeDb { prefix: "row" };
    provide Db = db;

    let r = use_db();
    print(f"returned: {r}");
    print(f"count: {Db.tally()}");
}
